The wavelength today and the wavelength at decoupling are related by $\frac{\lambda_0}{\lambda_{\rm dec}}
=
\frac{a_0}{a_{\rm dec}}
=
\frac{T_{\rm dec}}{T_0}.$ Decoupling is not mathematically instantaneous, but it is short enough compared with the subsequent history that one may assign it a characteristic scale factor and temperature. Here $T_0$ means the CMB temperature, not the kinetic temperature of intergalactic matter.

